## What the immersed boundary costs

The Taylor–Green control runs the identical grids with no geometry. At one GPU the geometry costs
a factor **{{ibm_cost}}×** in step time, and it is the pressure solve that pays: the cut-cell
operator needs **{{ibm_iters_ratio}}×** the iterations of the all-fluid one, on a matrix whose
coefficients span the aperture contrast of a dense bed.

## Permeability

Marched to steady state, the unit cell has $k/R^2 = {{k_over_R2}}$ ({{k_march_steps}} steps to a
relative tolerance of $10^{-5}$). Measured at {{k_runs}} points of the ladder, the estimates agree
to {{k_spread}} — the same physical answer from the single-GPU cell and from the tiled
{{w_top_gcells}}-billion-cell domain.

